<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parthenos (Chersonesus)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Parthenos, the Maiden, was the patron goddess of the Greek city of Chersonesus Taurica in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a>. Greek writers identified her with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artemis">Artemis</a> and with the virgin goddess of the Taurians, to whom, according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>, shipwrecked strangers were sacrificed. Her image appears on the city's coins, and its citizens swore their civic oath in her name together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeus">Zeus</a>, Earth and the Sun.</p></div>
